--TEST--
A `[limits]` value that is not a quantity stops the boot with E0601, and the program never runs — `rule:config/one-parser-for-the-boot-path-and-config-set`
--FILE nvs.toml--
[limits]
memory = "12 bananas"
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `12 bananas` is not a size, so the configuration is refused before this line runs.
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0601]: `limits.memory` is `12 bananas`, which is not a size
%A
